WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.636 --> 00:00:07.671
Russia bears responsibility

00:00:07.804 --> 00:00:09.506
for the incident.

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:10.374
&gt;&gt; Today volodymyr zelenskyy

00:00:10.474 --> 00:00:14.378
says he's convinced the missile

00:00:14.378 --> 00:00:17.314
that landed in Poland was not

00:00:17.447 --> 00:00:18.415
Ukrainian and has the doubts

00:00:18.548 --> 00:00:20.650
from his own commander.

00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:22.386
Matthew chance is at the site of

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:23.687
the strike and it's clear this

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.455
incident marks one of the

00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:27.324
biggest tests of the nato

00:00:27.457 --> 00:00:29.025
alliance in recent history.

00:00:29.159 --> 00:00:31.128
&gt;&gt; Reporter: A Russian made

00:00:31.261 --> 00:00:33.530
missile striking a nato ally and

00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:35.432
setting the world on edge, but

00:00:35.565 --> 00:00:38.602
it now seems the explosion that

00:00:38.735 --> 00:00:39.336
killed two Polish farmers here

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:42.005
was a tragic accident, not as

00:00:42.406 --> 00:00:44.508
feared ordered by the Kremlin.

00:00:44.641 --> 00:00:46.643
&gt;&gt; The incident most likely

00:00:46.777 --> 00:00:51.314
caused by Ukrainian air defense

00:00:51.448 --> 00:00:53.717
missile fired to the Ukrainian

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:54.651
territory against Russian cruise

00:00:54.785 --> 00:00:57.687
missile attacks.

00:00:57.821 --> 00:01:03.527
But let me be clear, this is not

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.160
Ukraine's fault.

00:01:04.428 --> 00:01:06.430
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Not Ukraine's fault

00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:07.731
because its military was

00:01:07.864 --> 00:01:11.034
defending against the barrage of

00:01:11.168 --> 00:01:14.805
Russian missiles targeting

00:01:14.938 --> 00:01:16.673
infrastructure and killing

00:01:16.807 --> 00:01:17.307
civilians.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:18.742
Among the victims was this

00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:20.444
69-year-old woman visiting her

00:01:20.444 --> 00:01:22.579
husband's grave in Kyiv when a

00:01:22.712 --> 00:01:25.515
piece of shrapnel tore through

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:27.451
her body and killed her.

00:01:27.584 --> 00:01:33.356
As wintersets in, it is reckless

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:35.425
abandon but what happens in

00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:37.661
Poland shows how dangerous that

00:01:37.794 --> 00:01:39.129
is for the whole world, too,

00:01:39.262 --> 00:01:40.964
while Ukrainian officials are

00:01:41.097 --> 00:01:42.799
redoubling request for more

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:43.934
advanced air defense systems

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.802
from the United States and

00:01:45.936 --> 00:01:46.436
Europe.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:50.907
They've also committed to C

00:01:51.041 --> 00:01:51.741
cooperating with an

00:01:51.875 --> 00:01:53.510
investigation and admitted the

00:01:53.643 --> 00:01:54.845
air defenses were active in the

00:01:54.978 --> 00:02:00.150
area but officials are clear,

00:02:00.484 --> 00:02:02.986
Russian president Vladimir Putin

00:02:03.119 --> 00:02:03.619
is responsible dragging

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.989
Ukrainians and a sleepily

00:02:06.122 --> 00:02:07.023
one-street Polish town into his

00:02:07.157 --> 00:02:13.930
war of choice.

00:02:14.064 --> 00:02:15.665
Jake, teams of specialists from

00:02:15.799 --> 00:02:17.634
both Poland and the united

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.469
States are still here trying to

00:02:19.603 --> 00:02:21.037
piece together the fragments of

00:02:21.171 --> 00:02:23.673
the missile that slammed into

00:02:23.807 --> 00:02:26.877
this isolated Polish village but

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:28.144
tonight, concerns that incident

00:02:28.512 --> 00:02:31.414
in a nato allied country,

00:02:31.548 --> 00:02:34.851
remember, may spark a broader

00:02:34.985 --> 00:02:37.320
conflict, definitely showing

00:02:37.454 --> 00:02:39.089
signs most definitely of easing.

00:02:39.222 --> 00:02:39.623
Jake.

00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:40.657
&gt;&gt; Matthew chance in Poland for

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:44.027
us.
Thank you so much.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.129
While Ukraine's president

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:47.364
volodymyr zelenskyy insists the

00:02:47.497 --> 00:02:49.032
missile was not Ukrainian, it

00:02:49.165 --> 00:02:52.536
was echoed in U.S. Intelligence

00:02:52.536 --> 00:02:53.036
earlier today.

00:02:53.103 --> 00:02:54.538
Take a listen.

00:02:54.538 --> 00:02:56.907
&gt;&gt; Our preliminary analysis

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.642
suggests that the incident most

00:02:58.775 --> 00:03:02.646
likely caused by Ukrainian air

00:03:02.779 --> 00:03:03.380
defense missile.

00:03:03.513 --> 00:03:07.050
&gt;&gt; CNN's Melissa bell is in

00:03:07.183 --> 00:03:07.851
Brussels for us now.

00:03:07.984 --> 00:03:10.086
She spent the day at nato

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:10.654
headquarters.

00:03:10.654 --> 00:03:12.556
Poland is considering invoking

00:03:12.622 --> 00:03:15.725
article 4 of the nato treaty

00:03:15.859 --> 00:03:17.561
that calls for consultation that

00:03:17.694 --> 00:03:18.662
can be invoked when any member

00:03:18.795 --> 00:03:20.230
state feels threatened in any

00:03:20.564 --> 00:03:23.733
way.
How is nato responding?

00:03:23.867 --> 00:03:25.669
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The messaing today

00:03:25.802 --> 00:03:27.604
was really in line with what

00:03:27.737 --> 00:03:28.572
president Biden had to say on

00:03:28.705 --> 00:03:30.807
his way out of the G 20 summit

00:03:30.941 --> 00:03:32.876
when he left Bali, which is very

00:03:33.009 --> 00:03:34.911
quickly while this investigation

00:03:35.045 --> 00:03:37.314
continues, this was not a

00:03:37.447 --> 00:03:38.815
missile fired by Russia really

00:03:38.949 --> 00:03:43.453
trying to tone things down,

00:03:43.587 --> 00:03:44.588
trying to stop anyone from

00:03:44.721 --> 00:03:45.589
getting too excited about this.

00:03:45.722 --> 00:03:47.023
We all arrived this morning Jake

00:03:47.157 --> 00:03:48.758
hearing about the potential

00:03:48.892 --> 00:03:50.594
invoking of article 4.

00:03:50.594 --> 00:03:52.596
That's the beginning of

00:03:52.696 --> 00:03:53.496
consultations and can lead to

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:54.130
article 5.

00:03:54.164 --> 00:03:55.665
That's the foundational

00:03:55.799 --> 00:03:57.434
principle of nato but of course,

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.436
what it means is an attack on

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:01.371
one country is an attack on all

00:04:01.504 --> 00:04:02.606
and it would very quickly lead

00:04:02.706 --> 00:04:04.074
to the kind of escalation that

00:04:04.207 --> 00:04:05.942
everyone is worried about ever

00:04:06.076 --> 00:04:08.144
since this invasion began and

00:04:08.278 --> 00:04:10.013
nato stepped up to the plate to

00:04:10.146 --> 00:04:10.714
help Ukraine.

00:04:10.847 --> 00:04:13.016
So today was really at nato

00:04:13.149 --> 00:04:14.117
headquarters trying to calm

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.352
everything down, not with

00:04:15.485 --> 00:04:16.620
standing what president

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.054
zelenskyy was going, was saying

00:04:18.188 --> 00:04:19.689
about what he believed has

00:04:19.823 --> 00:04:20.624
happened and we've been hearing

00:04:20.757 --> 00:04:23.627
that messaging fairly

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:24.194
consistently.

00:04:24.194 --> 00:04:26.630
Consider, also, Jake, that

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:28.898
extraordinary unity we've seen

00:04:29.032 --> 00:04:30.667
on the part of nato since this

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.869
conflict began, that we could

00:04:33.003 --> 00:04:35.071
have imagined a year ago would

00:04:35.205 --> 00:04:36.640
be severely tested and also,

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:37.907
Jake, things are going exactly

